breaking_changes.Adaptation_method:
To maintain the previous behavior and prevent errors due to excess arguments, add '.allowExcessArguments()' to your command definition before calling 'parse', as in:

program.option('-p, --port <number>', 'port number');
program.allowExcessArguments();
program.action((options) => {
  console.log(program.args);
});

Alternatively, explicitly specify accepted positional arguments using '.argument(...)' for each expected argument. Any excess arguments will then generate an error unless 'allowExcessArguments()' is enabled.

Update Option construction to use only supported flag formats. For short options, use a single character after a single dash (e.g., new Option('-a, --alpha')). For long options, use a single long option per Option (e.g., new Option('--example')). Do not provide multi-letter short flags (e.g., '-es') or multiple long flags (e.g., '--foo, --bar') in one Option construction if using v13.0.0. If you need multiple flags for the same option, declare separate Option instances for each, or, if using Commander 13.1.0 or later, check dual-long flag support. 

Examples:

// Before (invalid in v13.0.0, throws error):
new Option('-es, --ecmascript');
new Option('--foo, --bar');

// After (v13.0.0):
new Option('-e, --ecmascript');
// To support both --foo and --bar, create separate options or use Commander >=13.1.0 for dual long option support.

Refactor code to ensure that when using a Command instance with 'storeOptionsAsProperties: true', 'parse()' is only called once per Command instance lifecycle. When multiple parses are required, either set 'storeOptionsAsProperties: false' or recreate the Command instance between parses. Example adaptations:

// Avoid multiple parses with storeOptionsAsProperties: true
const cmd = new Command();
cmp.storeOptionsAsProperties = true;
cmp.parse(process.argv); // OK
// cmd.parse(['node', 'script.js', '--foo']); // Throws if called again

// Allow multiple parses with storeOptionsAsProperties: false or default
const cmd2 = new Command();
cmp2.parse(['node', 'script.js', '--foo']); // OK
cmp2.parse(['node', 'script.js', '--bar']); // OK
